# Phase 2 — Review Fixes & Improvements

## Summary
Executed fixes for all 7 findings (6 Major + 1 Minor) identified in the Phase 2 code review (`.agents/reviews/PHASE_2/review.md`).
The fixes address error propagation, ensemble confidence semantics, single-entity PyOD ML scoring, DuckDB SQL filter pushdown performance, explanation polish guardrail validation, reporting tool invocation tracking, and Matplotlib object-oriented chart styling.

## Date: 2026-07-25T18:52:00+05:30

## Files Modified & Summary of Fixes

| File | Fix Type | Change Description |
|------|----------|--------------------|
| `src/tools/detection/tool.py` | Major 1 | Added explicit error propagation if `FeatureTool` fails (`feat_res.status != "ok"`), returning `status="error"` instead of hiding failures under `status="ok"`. |
| `src/tools/detection/ensemble.py` | Major 2 | Updated ensemble confidence math to count distinct detector families agreed divided by total detector families evaluated (`distinct_detector_families / 6.0`), preventing multiple flags in one rule family from artificially inflating confidence. |
| `src/tools/detection/ml_scorer.py` | Major 3 | Added background population baseline sampling (`_generate_background_baseline`) when scoring target batches ($N < 20$), enabling single-entity lookups ("Is customer 4521 suspicious?") to fit PyOD `IForest` and `LOF` and return relative anomaly scores instead of 0.0 scores. |
| `src/tools/features/tool.py` | Major 4 | Replaced `SELECT * FROM transactions` full table scans with SQL-level filter pushdown: `WHERE timestamp >= cutoff` and `WHERE (sender_account_id IN (...) OR receiver_account_id IN (...))`, ensuring on-demand minimal data materialization from DuckDB. |
| `src/tools/explanation/tool.py` | Major 5 | Fully wired `enable_llm_polish` path to execute phrasing polish (`_apply_phrasing_polish`) and validate output against `verify_numeric_preservation()`, falling back to grounded text on numeric drift. |
| `src/tools/reporting/tool.py` | Major 6 | Updated tool invocation tracking to use `is not None` checks instead of boolean truthiness, and added support for explicit `tools_invoked` input override. |
| `src/tools/eda/charts.py` | Minor 1 | Removed global `plt.rcParams.update(...)` mutation in favor of per-figure object-oriented styling (`_style_figure(fig, axes)`). |
| `tests/test_tools/test_detection.py` | Tests | Added unit tests for feature error propagation, detector family confidence consensus, and single-entity PyOD ML lookup. |
| `tests/test_tools/test_explanation.py` | Tests | Added test for `enable_llm_polish=True` with numeric preservation guardrail validation. |
| `tests/test_tools/test_reporting.py` | Tests | Added tests for empty result payload tracking (`{}`) and explicit `tools_invoked` input override. |

